### YCR API — the F-001 station endpoints, the F-002 sign-in and administration endpoints, the
### F-003 route endpoints, the F-004 service endpoints and the F-005 timetable-version endpoints.
###
### Setup (README "Developer setup"): a dev signing key and Auth:AllowedOrigins:0 in user-secrets,
### and a first administrator from `YCR.Worker bootstrap-administrator`.
###
### Every /api/v1 endpoint except /auth/login and /auth/refresh needs a bearer token. Sign in,
### copy accessToken into @token below (it lives 15 minutes; refresh for a new one). The
### bootstrap and every administrator-set password are must-change: until POST /auth/password
### succeeds, everything but /auth/me, /auth/password, /auth/logout and /auth/refresh answers
### 403 Auth.PasswordChangeRequired (R26).
###
### The cookie endpoints (login, refresh, logout) check Origin (R9): each request below sends the
### allowed origin you configured. Without it: 403 Auth.OriginRejected.
###
### OpenAPI document (Development environment only): {{host}}/openapi/v1.json

@host = http://localhost:5080
@origin = http://localhost:5080
@token = paste-the-access-token-here
@refresh = paste-the-ycr_refresh-cookie-value-here
@stationId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@stationId2 = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@stationId3 = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@routeId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@serviceId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@scheduleVersionId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@userId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@sessionId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Liveness probe — expect 200. Anonymous.
GET {{host}}/health/live

### Readiness probe — expect 200, or 503 when the database is unreachable. Anonymous.
GET {{host}}/health/ready

### OpenAPI document — expect 200 in Development, 404 otherwise.
### Not served outside Development: the document maps every route and the permission each one
### requires, which a deployed instance has no reason to hand out.
GET {{host}}/openapi/v1.json

# ---- Sign-in (spec §6.1) ----------------------------------------------------------------------

### Sign in — 200 { accessToken, expiresAtUtc } and Set-Cookie ycr_refresh (HttpOnly; Secure;
### SameSite=Strict; Path=/api/v1/auth/refresh). Wrong password, unknown user, disabled or
### locked account: the same 401 Auth.InvalidCredentials. 429 Auth.TooManyRequests over the
### limits (5/min per username, 20/min per address).
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/login
Origin: {{origin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userName": "your.name",
  "password": "your password"
}

### Refresh — 200 with a new access token and a rotated cookie. A browser sends the cookie by
### itself; a REST client may not send a Secure cookie over http, so it is sent explicitly here.
### 409 Auth.RefreshSuperseded when this token was rotated within the last 20 s (another tab);
### 401 Auth.RefreshInvalid otherwise.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/refresh
Origin: {{origin}}
Cookie: ycr_refresh={{refresh}}

### Who am I — 200 { userId, userName, roles, permissions }.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Change own password — 204; revokes your other sessions. 400 Auth.PasswordRejected (12–128
### characters, not a common password), 422 Auth.CurrentPasswordIncorrect.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/password
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currentPassword": "your password",
  "newPassword": "a new password of 12 or more characters"
}

### Sign out — 204; revokes this session and expires the cookie.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/logout
Origin: {{origin}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

# ---- Administration (spec §6.2; SystemAdministrator's permissions) -----------------------------

### List staff accounts — users.read.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users?page=1&pageSize=50
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Read one — users.read. 404 Identity.UserNotFound.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{userId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create — users.manage. 201; the password is must-change. 400 Identity.InvalidUserName
### (3–50 of a-z 0-9 .), 400 Identity.PasswordRejected, 409 Identity.UserNameAlreadyExists.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userName": "new.clerk",
  "password": "an initial password",
  "roles": ["TicketOperator"]
}

### Replace roles — users.roles.manage. 422 Identity.CannotChangeOwnRoles,
### 422 Identity.LastAdministrator.
PUT {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{userId}}/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "roles": ["TicketOperator", "TicketInspector"]
}

### Disable — users.manage; revokes all the account's sessions. 422 Identity.CannotDisableOwnAccount,
### 422 Identity.LastAdministrator.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{userId}}/disable
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Enable — users.manage.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{userId}}/enable
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Unlock — users.manage; clears a lockout (10 failures lock for 15 minutes).
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{userId}}/unlock
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Administrator password reset — users.manage; must-change; revokes all sessions.
### 422 Identity.CannotResetOwnPassword (use /auth/password).
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{userId}}/password-reset
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "newPassword": "a temporary password"
}

### A user's sessions — users.read.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{userId}}/auth-sessions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Revoke one session — auth-sessions.revoke. 404 Identity.SessionNotFound.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth-sessions/{{sessionId}}/revoke
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### The role catalogue and each role's permissions — users.read. Grants change only by migration.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

# ---- Stations (F-001) -------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Create a station — stations.manage. 201 + Location, or 400 / 409 Network.StationCodeAlreadyExists.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/stations
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "INS",
  "nameEn": "Insein",
  "nameMy": "အင်းစိန်"
}

### Create a station with an invalid code — 400 Network.InvalidStationCode. The code rule (R3)
### lives only in StationCode and is provisional until OQ26 is answered.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/stations
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "in-s",
  "nameEn": "Insein",
  "nameMy": "အင်းစိန်"
}

### List stations — stations.read. 200 with { items, page, pageSize, totalCount }, ordered by code.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/stations?page=1&pageSize=50
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Read one station — stations.read. 200, or 404 Network.StationNotFound.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/stations/{{stationId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Deactivate a station — stations.manage. 204, 404 Network.StationNotFound, or
### 422 Network.StationAlreadyInactive. The row is retained, so the code is never reused (R3).
POST {{host}}/api/v1/stations/{{stationId}}/deactivate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

# ---- Routes (F-003) ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# A route is an ordered, immutable sequence of existing, active stations (OQ37/OQ38 provisional
# rulings). It is created whole, read, and deactivated; nothing else. There is no
# PUT /routes/{id}/stations and no PATCH: to change the network, create a new route and
# deactivate the old one. Set @stationId, @stationId2 and @stationId3 to three active stations.

### Create an open route with three stations — routes.manage. 201 + Location and { id }.
### Errors: 400 Common.ValidationFailed (missing field, missing isClosed, a stationId that is not a
### GUID, more than 200 stationIds); 400 Network.InvalidRouteCode / Network.InvalidRouteName;
### 409 Network.RouteCodeAlreadyExists (codes are never reused, inactive routes included);
### 422 Network.RouteStationNotFound / RouteStationInactive / RouteStationRepeated / RouteTooFewStations.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/routes
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "LOOP1",
  "nameEn": "Yangon Circular",
  "nameMy": "ရန်ကုန်မြို့ပတ်",
  "isClosed": false,
  "stationIds": ["{{stationId}}", "{{stationId2}}", "{{stationId3}}"]
}

### A closed route needs at least 3 stations — 422 Network.RouteTooFewStations. A closed route runs
### from its last station back to its first because isClosed says so; never repeat the first station.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/routes
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "LOOP2",
  "nameEn": "Too short",
  "nameMy": "တိုလွန်း",
  "isClosed": true,
  "stationIds": ["{{stationId}}", "{{stationId2}}"]
}

### A station twice in one sequence — 422 Network.RouteStationRepeated.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/routes
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "LOOP3",
  "nameEn": "Repeated",
  "nameMy": "ထပ်နေ",
  "isClosed": true,
  "stationIds": ["{{stationId}}", "{{stationId2}}", "{{stationId3}}", "{{stationId}}"]
}

### List routes — routes.read. 200 with { items, page, pageSize, totalCount }, ordered by code,
### inactive routes included; each item has stationCount. 400 Network.InvalidPageRequest over 200.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/routes?page=1&pageSize=50
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Read one route — routes.read. 200 with stations in position order, each showing the station's
### current code, names and isActive; or 404 Network.RouteNotFound.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/routes/{{routeId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Deactivate a route — routes.manage. 204, 404 Network.RouteNotFound. The row and its sequence are
### kept; deactivatedAtUtc is set.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/routes/{{routeId}}/deactivate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Deactivate it again — 422 Network.RouteAlreadyInactive; deactivatedAtUtc keeps its first value.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/routes/{{routeId}}/deactivate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

# ---- Services (F-004) -------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# A service is a named, directed run along one route: its stops in order, the days it operates and
# its effective period (OQ43-OQ50 provisional rulings). It is created whole, read, and withdrawn;
# nothing else. There is no PATCH (OQ48): to change a timetable, withdraw the service from a date D
# and create the same code from D.
#
# Set @routeId to an active, CLOSED route whose stations are @stationId, @stationId2, @stationId3
# in that order (create it above with "isClosed": true), and @serviceId from the first create below.
# Dates are YYYY-MM-DD in Asia/Yangon (Time:LocalTimeZone); "today" is the Yangon date. The dates
# below are examples: effectiveTo and withdrawFrom must not be earlier than today.

### Create a Forward service on the closed route — services.manage. 201 + Location and { id }.
### Errors: 400 Common.ValidationFailed (missing field, a GUID or date in another format, a day
### name that is not exactly Monday..Sunday, a repeated day, more than 200 stopStationIds);
### 400 Timetable.InvalidServiceCode / InvalidServiceName / InvalidEffectivePeriod;
### 422 Timetable.ServiceEffectiveToInPast / ServiceRouteNotFound / ServiceRouteInactive /
### ServiceStopNotOnRoute / ServiceStopRepeated / ServiceTooFewStops / ServiceStopsOutOfOrder /
### ServiceStopStationInactive; 409 Timetable.ServiceCodePeriodOverlap; 413 over 32 KiB.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/services
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "SV10",
  "nameEn": "Circular morning",
  "nameMy": "မနက်ပိုင်း",
  "routeId": "{{routeId}}",
  "direction": "Forward",
  "stopStationIds": ["{{stationId}}", "{{stationId2}}", "{{stationId3}}"],
  "operatingDays": ["Monday", "Tuesday", "Wednesday", "Thursday", "Friday"],
  "effectiveFrom": "2027-01-01"
}

### A wrap — services.manage. 201. On a closed route, Forward from the last station to the first
### is one step; on an open route the same stops are 422 Timetable.ServiceStopsOutOfOrder.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/services
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "SV11",
  "nameEn": "Circular wrap",
  "nameMy": "ပတ်ပြန်",
  "routeId": "{{routeId}}",
  "direction": "Forward",
  "stopStationIds": ["{{stationId3}}", "{{stationId}}"],
  "operatingDays": ["Saturday", "Sunday"],
  "effectiveFrom": "2027-01-01"
}

### A full circuit — services.manage. 201. Only on a closed route, the last stop may repeat the
### first: exactly one circuit, at least 3 distinct stations.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/services
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "SV12",
  "nameEn": "Full circuit",
  "nameMy": "တစ်ပတ်လည်",
  "routeId": "{{routeId}}",
  "direction": "Forward",
  "stopStationIds": ["{{stationId}}", "{{stationId2}}", "{{stationId3}}", "{{stationId}}"],
  "operatingDays": ["Monday"],
  "effectiveFrom": "2027-01-01",
  "effectiveTo": "2027-12-31"
}

### A stop out of order — 422 Timetable.ServiceStopsOutOfOrder: Forward 1 → 3 → 2 would pass the
### first stop again (more than one circuit).
POST {{host}}/api/v1/services
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "SV13",
  "nameEn": "Out of order",
  "nameMy": "အစီအစဉ်မမှန်",
  "routeId": "{{routeId}}",
  "direction": "Forward",
  "stopStationIds": ["{{stationId}}", "{{stationId3}}", "{{stationId2}}"],
  "operatingDays": ["Monday"],
  "effectiveFrom": "2027-01-01"
}

### The same code with an overlapping period — 409 Timetable.ServiceCodePeriodOverlap. SV10 runs
### from 2027-01-01, open-ended. Withdrawn services still count; one whose period never runs does not.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/services
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "SV10",
  "nameEn": "Circular morning",
  "nameMy": "မနက်ပိုင်း",
  "routeId": "{{routeId}}",
  "direction": "Reverse",
  "stopStationIds": ["{{stationId3}}", "{{stationId2}}", "{{stationId}}"],
  "operatingDays": ["Monday"],
  "effectiveFrom": "2027-02-01"
}

### List services — services.read. 200 with { items, page, pageSize, totalCount }, withdrawn ones
### included, ordered by code, then effectiveFrom, then id. 400 Timetable.InvalidPageRequest over 200.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/services?page=1&pageSize=50
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### List one route's services — services.read. 200.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/services?routeId={{routeId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Read one service — services.read. 200 with its stops in position order, showing the route's and
### each station's current values; or 404 Timetable.ServiceNotFound.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/services/{{serviceId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Withdraw — services.manage. 204: effectiveTo becomes the day before withdrawFrom (2027-05-31).
### Errors: 400 Common.ValidationFailed; 404 Timetable.ServiceNotFound; 409
### Timetable.ServiceChangedConcurrently; 422 Timetable.WithdrawalDateInPast (before today) /
### WithdrawalDoesNotShorten; 413 over 1 KiB.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/services/{{serviceId}}/withdraw
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "withdrawFrom": "2027-06-01"
}

### Withdraw to a later date — 422 Timetable.WithdrawalDoesNotShorten: a withdrawal only shortens.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/services/{{serviceId}}/withdraw
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "withdrawFrom": "2027-07-01"
}

### Timetable change, 1 of 2: withdraw SV10 from D = 2027-03-01 — 204 (effectiveTo 2027-02-28).
POST {{host}}/api/v1/services/{{serviceId}}/withdraw
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "withdrawFrom": "2027-03-01"
}

### Timetable change, 2 of 2: create SV10 again from D — 201, a new service id; the periods no
### longer overlap.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/services
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "SV10",
  "nameEn": "Circular morning",
  "nameMy": "မနက်ပိုင်း",
  "routeId": "{{routeId}}",
  "direction": "Forward",
  "stopStationIds": ["{{stationId}}", "{{stationId3}}"],
  "operatingDays": ["Monday", "Tuesday", "Wednesday", "Thursday", "Friday"],
  "effectiveFrom": "2027-03-01"
}

# ---- Schedule versions (F-005) ---------------------------------------------------------------
#
# A version is the whole network's timetable from a start date until the next published version's
# start date: every listed service with its stop times, HH:mm (00:00-23:59). Stop 1 has only a
# departure, the last stop only an arrival, every other stop both; arrival ≤ departure at a stop;
# each arrival later than the previous departure. A draft is created whole and never edited; it is
# published, or discarded; a published version can be cancelled only before its start date.
# BUSINESS DECISIONS — provisional tech-lead rulings (OQ51-OQ60), not Myanma Railways answers.
#
# Set @serviceId to a service from the section above (effective on the start date below; the
# example uses SV10 with its two stops) and @scheduleVersionId from the create below.

### Create a draft — schedules.manage. 201 + Location and { id, number }.
### Errors: 400 Common.ValidationFailed (effectiveFrom not YYYY-MM-DD, services missing, a null
### entry, serviceId not a GUID, stopTimes missing, position missing or < 1, more than 250 services,
### more than 200 stop times for one service, more than 10,000 in total); 400
### Timetable.InvalidScheduleVersionName / InvalidTimetableTime; 422
### Timetable.ScheduleVersionEffectiveFromInPast / EmptyScheduleVersionNotInFuture /
### ScheduleServiceNotFound / ScheduleServiceRepeated / ScheduleServiceNotEffective /
### ScheduleStopNotInService / ScheduleStopTimesIncomplete / ScheduleStopTimeUnexpected /
### ScheduleDwellNegative / ScheduleTimesNotIncreasing; 413 over 2 MiB.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/schedules/versions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nameEn": "Timetable from March 2027",
  "nameMy": "အချိန်ဇယား",
  "effectiveFrom": "2027-03-01",
  "services": [
    {
      "serviceId": "{{serviceId}}",
      "stopTimes": [
        { "position": 1, "departure": "06:00" },
        { "position": 2, "arrival": "06:40" }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

### Read it — schedules.read. 200 with number, names, effectiveFrom, status and each listed
### service's current values; or 404 Timetable.ScheduleVersionNotFound.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/schedules/versions/{{scheduleVersionId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### One service's times — schedules.read. 200 with stops in position order, each station's current
### code and names, arrival/departure as HH:mm or null; 404 Timetable.ScheduleServiceNotInVersion.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/schedules/versions/{{scheduleVersionId}}/services/{{serviceId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### List — schedules.read. 200 with { items, page, pageSize, totalCount }, ordered by number;
### status is exactly Draft, Published, Discarded or Cancelled (else 400 Common.ValidationFailed);
### 400 Timetable.InvalidPageRequest over 200.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/schedules/versions?page=1&pageSize=50&status=Draft
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Publish — schedules.manage. 204. Errors: 404; 409 Timetable.ScheduleVersionEffectiveFromTaken
### (another published version starts that day) / ScheduleVersionChangedConcurrently; 422
### Timetable.ScheduleVersionNotDraft / ScheduleVersionEffectiveFromInPast /
### EmptyScheduleVersionNotInFuture / ScheduleServiceNotEffective (listed services are re-checked).
POST {{host}}/api/v1/schedules/versions/{{scheduleVersionId}}/publish
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### In force on a date — schedules.read. 200 with runsOnDate per listed service (its own period
### and weekdays); 404 Timetable.ScheduleVersionNotInForce before the first published version;
### 400 Common.ValidationFailed without a YYYY-MM-DD date.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/schedules/versions/in-force?date=2027-03-01
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### A second draft on the same start date — 201. Set @scheduleVersionId to its id and run the
### publish request above again: 409 Timetable.ScheduleVersionEffectiveFromTaken while the first
### stays published (start dates are unique among published versions).
POST {{host}}/api/v1/schedules/versions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nameEn": "Timetable from March 2027, second draft",
  "nameMy": "အချိန်ဇယား",
  "effectiveFrom": "2027-03-01",
  "services": []
}

### Cancel a published version before its start date — schedules.manage. 204; it is kept and never
### applies. On or after its start date: 422 Timetable.ScheduleVersionAlreadyEffective; not
### published: 422 Timetable.ScheduleVersionNotPublished.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/schedules/versions/{{scheduleVersionId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Discard a draft — schedules.manage. 204; kept and readable, never applies. Not a draft: 422
### Timetable.ScheduleVersionNotDraft.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/schedules/versions/{{scheduleVersionId}}/discard
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### An empty version starting today — 422 Timetable.EmptyScheduleVersionNotInFuture (an empty
### version, a network-wide suspension, must start after today, so it can always be cancelled).
### Replace the date with today's Asia/Yangon date.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/schedules/versions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nameEn": "Suspension",
  "nameMy": "ရပ်ဆိုင်း",
  "effectiveFrom": "2026-10-01",
  "services": []
}

### Withdraw a service a published version lists — services.manage. 422
### Timetable.ServiceInPublishedScheduleVersion while that version applies on or after withdrawFrom
### (publish a version without the service first, then withdraw it from that version's start date).
POST {{host}}/api/v1/services/{{serviceId}}/withdraw
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "withdrawFrom": "2027-04-01"
}
